  "decision_conditions": [
    "The works approved by this Listed Building Consent must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this decision notice. \rReason: To comply with S.51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLocation Plan\rE7991-GA-LP-BP\rE7991-EX-E1\rE7991-EX-E2\rE7991-EX-E3\rE7991-EX-GD\rE7991-GA-GD\rE7991-GA-E1\rE7991-GA-E2\rE7991-GA-E3\rDesign, Access & Heritage Statement\rFlood Risk Assessment\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Prior to use, sample(s) of the infill stone to be used on the external finishes shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The works shall be implemented in accordance with the approved details and permanently retained as such.\r\rReason: In order to safeguard the special architectural and historic interest of the building.\r",
    "Prior to the commencement of works, a sample panel no smaller than 30cm² shall be provided for inspection on-site to show areas of new brickwork and approved in writing by the local planning authority. This panel shall indicate the brick size, colour, texture and bond together with mortar mix, joint size, colour and pointing profile.\r\rUpon approval the sample panels shall be retained on site for reference for the duration of works unless otherwise agreed in writing with the local planning authority. The works shall be implemented in accordance with the approved details and shall be permanently maintained as such.\r\rReason: In order to safeguard the special architectural and historic interest of the building.\r"
  ],
